            {
                "box": {
                    "annotation_name": "Category",
                    "fontsize": 12.0,
                    "hint": "the categories of the glossary; choose one to see its terms",
                    "id": "obj-15",
                    "items": [ "Testing basics", ",", "Asserts in depth", ",", "Expression helpers", ",", "Signals and Jitter", ",", "Running suites", ",", "Results and CI", ",", "Linting" ],
                    "maxclass": "umenu",
                    "numinlets": 1,
                    "numoutlets": 3,
                    "outlettype": [ "int", "", "" ],
                    "parameter_enable": 0,
                    "patching_rect": [ 20.0, 620.0, 250.0, 22.0 ],
                    "presentation": 1,
                    "presentation_rect": [ 20.0, 94.0, 520.0, 22.0 ]
                }
            },
            {
                "box": {
                    "fontface": 2,
                    "id": "obj-17",
                    "maxclass": "comment",
                    "numinlets": 1,
                    "numoutlets": 0,
                    "patching_rect": [ 280.0, 660.0, 160.0, 20.0 ],
                    "text": "the category menu"
                }
            },
            {
                "box": {
                    "id": "obj-18",
                    "maxclass": "newobj",
                    "numinlets": 2,
                    "numoutlets": 5,
                    "outlettype": [ "dictionary", "", "", "", "" ],
                    "patching_rect": [ 20.0, 700.0, 250.0, 22.0 ],
                    "saved_object_attributes": {
                        "legacy": 1,
                        "parameter_enable": 0,
                        "parameter_mappable": 0
                    },
                    "text": "dict mUnit-glossary mUnit-glossary.json"
                }
            },
            {
                "box": {
                    "id": "obj-19",
                    "linecount": 3,
                    "maxclass": "comment",
                    "numinlets": 1,
                    "numoutlets": 0,
                    "patching_rect": [ 20.0, 730.0, 420.0, 47.0 ],
                    "text": "The loader: the second argument is the file, found through the search path because the package's misc folder is on it. Every other [dict mUnit-glossary] shares its contents; each lookup has its own so the replies stay apart."
                }
            },
            {
                "box": {
                    "id": "obj-20",
                    "linecount": 5,
                    "maxclass": "comment",
                    "numinlets": 1,
                    "numoutlets": 0,
                    "patching_rect": [ 480.0, 20.0, 420.0, 74.0 ],
                    "text": "2. A category is chosen. Right to left, the trigger stores the category's index in every [combine] that builds a path into the dict (their cold inlets), then fires the one that counts categories[i]::terms. That loop asks for each term by index and groups the names into one tabs message for the terms tab. Last, the first term is chosen."
                }
            },
            {
                "box": {
                    "id": "obj-21",
                    "maxclass": "newobj",
                    "numinlets": 1,
                    "numoutlets": 9,
                    "outlettype": [ "int", "int", "int", "int", "int", "int", "int", "int", "int" ],
                    "patching_rect": [ 480.0, 140.0, 103.0, 22.0 ],
                    "text": "t 0 i i i i i i i i"
                }
            },
            {
                "box": {
                    "annotation_name": "Terms",
                    "fontsize": 12.0,
                    "hint": "the terms of the category; click one to read it",
                    "id": "obj-34",
                    "maxclass": "tab",
                    "numinlets": 1,
                    "numoutlets": 3,
                    "outlettype": [ "int", "", "" ],
                    "parameter_enable": 0,
                    "patching_rect": [ 480.0, 620.0, 420.0, 98.0 ],
                    "presentation": 1,
                    "presentation_rect": [ 20.0, 128.0, 520.0, 98.0 ],
                    "rounded": 4.0,
                    "tabs": [ "test", "assert", "unit under test", "expression", "expected versus actual", "verdict", "suite", "fixture", "repeatable", "flaky test", "timeout", "skip and only", "test start", "teardown" ]
                }
            },
            {
                "box": {
                    "fontface": 2,
                    "id": "obj-35",
                    "maxclass": "comment",
                    "numinlets": 1,
                    "numoutlets": 0,
                    "patching_rect": [ 920.0, 660.0, 120.0, 20.0 ],
                    "text": "the terms tab"
                }
            },
            {
                "box": {
                    "id": "obj-36",
                    "linecount": 4,
                    "maxclass": "comment",
                    "numinlets": 1,
                    "numoutlets": 0,
                    "patching_rect": [ 940.0, 20.0, 420.0, 60.0 ],
                    "text": "3. A term is chosen. The tab's index goes, right to left, into the [combine]s that only store it (the buttons' actions and labels, the related terms) and then into the three that fetch at once: the definition here, the related terms (4) and the Go to buttons (5). The tab's own symbol is the title."
                }
            },
            {
                "box": {
                    "id": "obj-37",
                    "maxclass": "newobj",
                    "numinlets": 1,
                    "numoutlets": 6,
                    "outlettype": [ "int", "int", "int", "int", "int", "int" ],
                    "patching_rect": [ 624.0, 135.0, 160.0, 22.0 ],
                    "text": "t i i i i i i"
                }
            },
            {
                "box": {
                    "bgcolor": [ 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0 ],
                    "border": 0.0,
                    "fontsize": 12.0,
                    "id": "obj-43",
                    "linecount": 3,
                    "maxclass": "textedit",
                    "nosymquotes": 1,
                    "numinlets": 1,
                    "numoutlets": 4,
                    "outlettype": [ "", "int", "", "" ],
                    "parameter_enable": 0,
                    "patching_rect": [ 551.0, 351.0, 420.0, 80.0 ],
                    "presentation": 1,
                    "presentation_linecount": 3,
                    "presentation_rect": [ 20.0, 266.0, 520.0, 90.0 ],
                    "readonly": 1,
                    "text": "The outcome of an assert: pass, fail or skipped. The verdicts of every assert in a suite add up to the verdict of the run: Passed when nothing failed, Failed otherwise. Skipped asserts count for neither."
                }
            },
            {
                "box": {
                    "id": "obj-44",
                    "maxclass": "newobj",
                    "numinlets": 1,
                    "numoutlets": 1,
                    "outlettype": [ "" ],
                    "patching_rect": [ 680.5, 739.0, 72.0, 22.0 ],
                    "text": "prepend set"
                }
            },
            {
                "box": {
                    "bgcolor": [ 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0 ],
                    "border": 0.0,
                    "fontface": 1,
                    "fontsize": 16.0,
                    "id": "obj-45",
                    "maxclass": "textedit",
                    "nosymquotes": 1,
                    "numinlets": 1,
                    "numoutlets": 4,
                    "outlettype": [ "", "int", "", "" ],
                    "parameter_enable": 0,
                    "patching_rect": [ 680.5, 775.0, 420.0, 30.0 ],
                    "presentation": 1,
                    "presentation_rect": [ 20.0, 236.0, 520.0, 26.0 ],
                    "readonly": 1,
                    "text": "verdict"
                }
            },
            {
                "box": {
                    "fontface": 2,
                    "id": "obj-46",
                    "maxclass": "comment",
                    "numinlets": 1,
                    "numoutlets": 0,
                    "patching_rect": [ 657.0, 445.0, 300.0, 20.0 ],
                    "text": "the definition and, above it, the term"
                }
            },
            {
                "box": {
                    "id": "obj-47",
                    "linecount": 3,
                    "maxclass": "comment",
                    "numinlets": 1,
                    "numoutlets": 0,
                    "patching_rect": [ 940.0, 82.0, 420.0, 47.0 ],
                    "text": "4. Related terms: count categories[i]::terms[j]::also, clear the line, then fetch each name, put a dot in front of it, group them and join them into one line of text. A term with no related terms leaves the line empty."
                }
            },
            {
                "box": {
                    "bgcolor": [ 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0 ],
                    "border": 0.0,
                    "fontsize": 12.0,
                    "id": "obj-63",
                    "maxclass": "textedit",
                    "nosymquotes": 1,
                    "numinlets": 1,
                    "numoutlets": 4,
                    "outlettype": [ "", "int", "", "" ],
                    "parameter_enable": 0,
                    "patching_rect": [ 653.0, 315.0, 420.0, 22.0 ],
                    "presentation": 1,
                    "presentation_rect": [ 20.0, 380.0, 520.0, 20.0 ],
                    "readonly": 1,
                    "text": "· assert · suite · skip and only",
                    "textcolor": [ 0.45, 0.45, 0.47, 1.0 ]
                }
            },
            {
                "box": {
                    "id": "obj-64",
                    "linecount": 4,
                    "maxclass": "comment",
                    "numinlets": 1,
                    "numoutlets": 0,
                    "patching_rect": [ 1369.0, 20.0, 420.0, 60.0 ],
                    "text": "5. Go to: count the see entries and fetch each label into the buttons tab. A click fetches that entry's action, a verb and a target: help opens a help patcher and load a patch, through [pcontrol]; readme opens that section of the manual on GitHub and url a web page, through the browser."
